# Shadow Hacker — Changelog

## v2.0.0 (2026)

### Rebrand
- Full rebrand from lscript / Hak9 → Shadow Hacker
- Launch command: `shadow` (symlink in /usr/local/bin)
- New hooded-figure ASCII art banner with colour-cycling green code rain
- Main text and logo colours configurable via Settings menu

### Menus added
- **Reconnaissance** — RustScan, Netdiscover, OpenVAS, Angry IP Scanner,
  Routersploit, masscan, Eternal Scanner, Netattack2, Smart TV Discovery,
  HexStrike AI
- **Bluetooth Tools** — bluetoothctl, BTScanner, Bluelog, Spooftooph,
  Bettercap BLE, L2ping, Wireless Inventory, BLE Toy Lab
- **Remote Access additions** — PAYGEN, revshellgen, InternalAllTheThings
- **WiFi additions** — Sparrow-WiFi
- **Information Gathering additions** — Wireshark shortcut (w)

### PentestGPT integration
- Banner status line shows ACTIVE / NO KEY / OFF
- `pgpt` command from any prompt opens setup/launch
- `?` in any tool menu triggers context-aware PentestGPT assist
- API key stored in settings/openai_key.txt (chmod 600)

### Tor / identity
- `ni` shortcut from main menu requests new TorGhost identity
- Banner shows live public IP and Tor status
- TorGhost installed from github.com/INTELEON404/torghost.git

### Keyboard shortcuts (lh*)
- `lh1` → scripts/handshake-helper — WPA handshake capture
- `lh2` → scripts/deauth-helper    — Deauth attack helper
- `lh3` → scripts/monitor-mode     — Monitor mode toggle
- `lh4` → scripts/wpa-scan         — WPA network scan
- All four launch in a side terminal via gnome-terminal

### MITM scripts renamed
- ls/l131.sh → mitm/arp-spoof-fwd.sh
- ls/l132.sh → mitm/arp-spoof-rev.sh
- ls/l133.sh → mitm/dns2proxy.sh
- All MITM dispatch references updated to new paths

### Terminal auto-resize
- Each menu resizes terminal on open (wifi 45×110, website 50×120,
  bluetooth 42×105, recon 42×105, remote/info 48×115, other 42×105)

### Tools replaced
- Dracnmap (unmaintained) → RustScan
- nWatch (no GitHub) → masscan
- Netattack3/Gameye98 → Netattack2 (chrizator/netattack2)
- anonym8 check → TorGhost check

### Fixes
- TorGhost enable/disable wrapped in subshell (preserves working dir)
- btscanner now runs rfkill unblock + hciconfig hci0 up before launch
- Removed terms-of-use gate (IAGREE.txt) that blocked startup
- Fixed scan command (arp-scan pipe/tee)
- Netattack updated to python3/pip3
- Bluetooth tools rebuilt for modern Kali (hcitool deprecated)
- Window resize on launch: 40 rows × 95 cols
- install.sh: progress bar, dynamic RustScan .deb from GitHub releases API

### Project structure
- bin/hak9         → bin/shadowhacker
- hak/hak1–hak43  → scripts/ (descriptive names)
- ls/l131–133.sh  → mitm/ (arp-spoof-fwd/rev, dns2proxy)
- /root/recon     → /root/shadowhacker
